#import "main-defs.typ": *

= Generalities <ch:generalities>

#source(222)
In this chapter we describe the common background of the Chevalley groups over
rings for the rest of the paper. Most of the facts we mention are quite familiar
but to the best of my knowledge have never been collected in one place. Our
general references for the root systems and semi-simple Lie algebras are
#citation[@bib:Bourbaki2002, @bib:Bourbaki1975, @bib:Humphreys1980]\; for the
classical groups #citation[@bib:Artin1957, @bib:Dieudonne1971, @bib:Hahn1989b,
  @bib:McDonald1978, @bib:McDonald1976, @bib:OMeara1974, @bib:OMeara1978,
  @bib:Zalesski1985]\; for the Chevalley groups #citation[@bib:Borel1970,
  @bib:Carter1965, @bib:Carter1972a, @bib:Carter1972b, @bib:Carter1985,
  @bib:Humphreys1980, @bib:Steinberg1967, @bib:Seligman1967, @bib:Taddei1985]\;
for the algebraic groups #citation[@bib:Borel1969, @bib:Chevalley1956,
  @bib:Hahn1989a, @bib:Springer1981, @bib:Springer1989]\; for the affine group
schemes #citation[@bib:Abe1980, @bib:Demazure1970, @bib:Demazure1980,
  @bib:Demazure1971, @bib:Jantzen1987, @bib:Waterhouse1979]\; for the algebraic
K-theory #citation[@bib:Bak1981, @bib:Bass1964, @bib:Bass1968, @bib:Bass1973a,
  @bib:Milnor1971, @bib:Suslin1985].
